# What releasing needs to know. Copy this to .env, fill in the blanks, and never commit it --
# .gitignore already refuses to. Building and testing a checkout needs none of this; only
# `make publish` reads it.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#     $EDITOR .env
#     scripts/env.sh --check
#
# A runner has no .env. It is handed the same names by its own secret store, and every lane
# past scripts/env.sh reads only the environment -- so the two machines run the same code.

# The Apple Developer Program team the signing identities belong to, and the identifier both
# apps are registered under. One identifier, two platforms, one record in App Store Connect.
FEDIQO_TEAM_ID=J83AK3D9HB
FEDIQO_BUNDLE_ID=dev.mini-poc.fediqo

# Then one of two ways to sign in to Apple. Fill in either group, whole; the key wins where
# both are there.
#
# --- the key: works with nobody watching -------------------------------------------------
#
# From Users and Access -> Integrations -> App Store Connect API, on the Team Keys tab. The
# role has to be App Manager: a Developer can neither create a provisioning profile nor
# upload a build.
#
# The .p8 is offered for download exactly once. It is kept here as base64 rather than as a
# path, because a path is a thing only a laptop has -- base64 is a string, and a string is
# what a runner's secret store can hold.
#
#     base64 -i AuthKey_XXXXXXXXXX.p8 | tr -d '\n'
ASC_KEY_ID=
ASC_ISSUER_ID=
ASC_KEY_P8_BASE64=

# --- the Apple ID: works today, and asks a person for a second factor --------------------
#
# The fallback, for a laptop with a person sitting at it. Apple's two-factor session lasts
# about a month and can only be renewed by answering a prompt, so this way never survives a
# runner -- which is the whole reason the key above exists.
#
# The password is an app-specific one from appleid.apple.com, not the account password. The
# name is fastlane's own and cannot be spelled differently.
FEDIQO_APPLE_ID=
FASTLANE_APPLE_APPLICATION_SPECIFIC_PASSWORD=

# Where the certificates and profiles live, encrypted. The repository is shared with other
# projects on the same team; match keeps them apart by bundle identifier.
MATCH_GIT_URL=git@github.com:cmj0121/fastlane-match.git

# The passphrase that repository is encrypted with. Leave it blank on a machine that has run
# match before -- it is in the keychain, and match will ask there. A runner has no keychain,
# so a runner has to be told.
MATCH_PASSWORD=

# Only a runner needs this: cloning over HTTPS where there is no ssh key to clone with.
#     printf 'x-access-token:%s' "$TOKEN" | base64
MATCH_GIT_BASIC_AUTHORIZATION=
